  </div>

  <h2 id="salary">What it actually pays</h2>
  <p>
    India UX salary data varies widely by source, city, and company type, but the pattern across current
    listings is consistent: growth tracks shipped, measurable outcomes far more than it tracks years of
    tenure or a degree name by itself.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>Typical range</th>
          <th>What moves it</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {salaryRows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Stage">{row.stage}</td>
            <td data-label="Typical range">{row.range}</td>
            <td data-label="What moves it">{row.note}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="protocol-note">
    Ranges are directional, drawn from current India-focused salary sources including
    <a href="https://www.glassdoor.co.in/Salaries/ui-ux-designer-salary-SRCH_KO0,14.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Glassdoor</a>
    and <a href="https://www.payscale.com/research/IN/Job=UX_Designer/Salary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PayScale</a>,
    and will vary by city, company size, and individual portfolio strength.
  </p>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Mistakes that stall the path</h2>
  <div class="protocol-stack">
